DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ffrroomm prints out the mail header lines from the invoker's mailbox.

     The options are as follows:

     --ff _f_i_l_e
             The supplied file is examined instead of the invoker's mailbox.
             If the --ff option is used, the _u_s_e_r argument should not be used.

     --ss _s_e_n_d_e_r
             Only mail from addresses containing the supplied string are
             printed.

     If _u_s_e_r is given, the _u_s_e_r's mailbox is examined instead of the invoker's
     own mailbox.  (Privileges are required.)

EENNVVIIRROONNMMEENNTT
     ffrroomm utilizes the LOGNAME, MAIL, and USER environment variables.

     If the MAIL environment variable is set, its value is used as the path to
     the user's mail spool.

FFIILLEESS
     /var/mail/*

